WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:04.570
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:04.570 --> 00:08.200
Omoi wa kouya o yuku

00:08.200 --> 00:16.130
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

00:21.280 --> 00:27.790
Yaketsuku hizashi no moto kimi wa nani omou?

00:27.790 --> 00:33.730
Urei no hitomi wa ima nani o utsusu?

00:33.730 --> 00:42.670
Mayowazu ni irareru no nara
step by step tayasui darou

00:42.670 --> 00:47.440
Kaze no you ni

00:47.440 --> 00:50.510
Ikusen no namida o koe

00:50.510 --> 00:54.120
Akatsuki no kouya o yuku

00:54.120 --> 01:00.560
Itsuka kizu wa ieru kara saa trust myself

01:00.560 --> 01:07.360
Don't be afraid kawaru koto wa
osoreru koto ja nai

01:07.360 --> 01:13.470
Kimi ga kimi de aru naraba will be with you

01:13.470 --> 01:20.210
Odayaka na hi o yume-mite

01:20.210 --> 01:27.440
Michi-naki tabiji wa tsuzuku

01:40.200 --> 01:42.360
Welcome!

01:42.360 --> 01:44.800
Please enjoy your time at Amigo Tacos!

01:47.540 --> 01:51.560
Food, clothing, and shelter
are important to human beings.

02:19.230 --> 02:22.340
- How did it go?
- It ticks me off!

02:22.340 --> 02:24.140
So it didn't work out.

02:24.140 --> 02:26.770
Ellis, how much do you have on you?

02:31.680 --> 02:34.270
We won't even be able to buy bread with this.

02:37.290 --> 02:39.750
That damn machine woman!

02:39.750 --> 02:41.880
She plays way dirty!

02:49.700 --> 02:53.600
Did you take care of that matter for me?

02:53.600 --> 02:55.770
For your verification.

02:55.770 --> 02:59.640
All bank accounts have been suspended.

02:59.640 --> 03:03.680
Now, Nadie will be unable
to withdraw a single peso.

03:03.680 --> 03:06.480
Your instructions, please.

03:06.480 --> 03:08.250
We're finished now.

03:08.250 --> 03:09.620
What?

03:09.620 --> 03:11.920
Is there some problem?

03:11.920 --> 03:17.430
No, I was just under the impression
that you would move on to negotiate.

03:17.430 --> 03:23.970
Hitting her in the pocketbook
won't induce Nadie to part with Ellis.

03:23.970 --> 03:25.760
Then, why?

03:29.240 --> 03:32.540
To put it nicely, to educate her.

03:32.540 --> 03:36.340
To put it meanly, revenge, I suppose.

03:37.850 --> 03:39.510
What's this?

03:41.780 --> 03:43.380
Your payment.

03:43.380 --> 03:48.820
15% has been added on top of what
you demanded when we hired you.

03:48.820 --> 03:50.430
What's going on here?

03:50.430 --> 03:52.890
Your contract ends today.

03:52.890 --> 03:56.300
Hold on a minute! This is too sudden!

03:56.300 --> 03:58.230
I'm grateful to you.

03:58.230 --> 04:00.840
For protecting Ellis until today.

04:00.840 --> 04:02.700
What's going to happen to her?

04:02.700 --> 04:05.640
I have no need to tell you that.

04:05.640 --> 04:08.770
Stay out of her business from now on.

04:15.520 --> 04:16.850
You can have it back.

04:16.850 --> 04:19.850
- So, there you have it.
- Wait.

04:19.850 --> 04:23.320
I've made up my mind.

04:23.320 --> 04:27.330
That I'm going to stay by Ellis's side.

04:27.330 --> 04:32.860
I want her to know just how naive
her decision was back there.

04:41.780 --> 04:43.340
None of that now.

04:43.340 --> 04:47.650
We need a more quick and
easy way to make money.

04:47.650 --> 04:49.650
I'll do it.

04:49.650 --> 04:51.310
How?

04:56.990 --> 04:57.990
The end.

04:57.990 --> 05:04.070
Ooh! Incredible! Never before
have I seen such a fantastic illusion!

05:04.070 --> 05:06.730
Okay, admission fees here, please.

05:18.050 --> 05:20.780
Oh, man...

05:20.780 --> 05:23.350
Crispy nachos.

05:23.350 --> 05:25.750
I should've accepted the payment back there

05:25.750 --> 05:28.560
instead of trying to act cool.

05:28.560 --> 05:30.760
Piping hot enchiladas.

05:30.760 --> 05:33.530
No, no. If I had accepted that money,

05:33.530 --> 05:36.030
I would've regretted it for a hundred
lifetimes to come and then some!

05:36.030 --> 05:39.400
Tender cochinita pibil.

05:40.540 --> 05:44.670
Sweet, sweet banana chimichangas.

05:44.670 --> 05:47.980
Ellis, I appreciate the sentiment,

05:47.980 --> 05:49.880
but doesn't that make you
feel even more hungry?

05:49.880 --> 05:52.950
- Tacos.
- You're still going to keep at it?

05:52.950 --> 05:55.780
No, that.

05:59.650 --> 06:02.090
What about the taco, taco, tacos?

06:02.090 --> 06:03.890
They have a poster up.

06:03.890 --> 06:06.360
It says they're hiring.

06:06.360 --> 06:08.700
Really?! Where?

06:08.700 --> 06:10.100
See?

06:13.030 --> 06:15.840
I'm amazed that you can
read something so far away.

06:15.840 --> 06:18.900
Because I'm not normal.

06:20.840 --> 06:22.580
That...

06:22.580 --> 06:25.580
...might not be something
you want to mention too often.

06:25.580 --> 06:27.450
Yessir.

06:35.590 --> 06:38.860
Yum. I missed my chance to have lunch,

06:38.860 --> 06:40.600
so excuse me for doing this while I eat.

06:40.600 --> 06:41.800
Certainly.

06:41.800 --> 06:45.530
Let's see. Nadie is?

06:45.530 --> 06:49.400
- That's me.
- And you're Ellis?

06:49.400 --> 06:52.500
- Yes.
- Oh, that's mine...

06:54.880 --> 06:56.780
It's delicious!

06:58.150 --> 07:02.880
I've never had such a delicious taco in my life!

07:02.880 --> 07:04.920
I-I apologize.

07:04.920 --> 07:08.620
She may not look it, but she
hasn't had the best upbringing.

07:08.620 --> 07:11.160
- You're hired!
- What?

07:11.160 --> 07:13.690
Our tacos are delicious, aren't they?

07:13.690 --> 07:14.860
Yes.

07:14.860 --> 07:16.860
You bet they are, you bet they are.

07:16.860 --> 07:19.100
The truth is, just between you and me,

07:19.100 --> 07:22.800
I add a little something to the
sauce that the company sends me.

07:22.800 --> 07:27.480
It's my own sense of
perfectionism and pride, as it were.

07:27.480 --> 07:29.570
Wow, you're right!

07:32.050 --> 07:34.650
- It's delicious!
- Right?

07:34.650 --> 07:37.620
I put honey in there for some subtle flavor.

07:37.620 --> 07:39.120
Honey?

07:39.120 --> 07:41.660
Oh! I can taste it in there!

07:41.660 --> 07:43.590
It's definitely there!

07:45.530 --> 07:47.730
It's really delicious.

07:47.730 --> 07:49.860
You're hired, too.

07:58.670 --> 08:00.810
Welcome!

08:00.810 --> 08:03.210
Please enjoy your time at Amigo Tacos!

08:03.210 --> 08:06.110
Nadie, your smile is too big.

08:06.110 --> 08:09.150
- Yes, sir.
- Ellis, you need to smile more.

08:09.150 --> 08:10.880
Okay.

08:12.720 --> 08:14.120
Right.

08:16.160 --> 08:19.030
What would you like to order?

08:19.030 --> 08:22.100
Hey, I can't order unless I have a menu.

08:22.100 --> 08:24.890
Oh, right.

08:28.670 --> 08:32.870
Put down the glass here
and be cheerful and energetic.

08:34.040 --> 08:36.680
Water!

08:36.680 --> 08:39.940
You have to do it more softly.

08:45.790 --> 08:47.860
Water.

08:47.860 --> 08:51.260
No, that's not what I meant...

08:55.630 --> 08:57.830
Allow me to read back your order.

08:57.830 --> 09:03.910
Two Amigo Sets. And the drinks
are orange juice and coffee, correct?

09:03.910 --> 09:06.840
Then, please wait, it'll be just a bit.

09:06.840 --> 09:09.740
Looks like she's beginning
to pull it together somehow.

09:16.620 --> 09:18.150
Sorry about that.

09:18.150 --> 09:20.310
My hand just slipped.

09:23.560 --> 09:26.160
- Are you okay?
- With what?

09:26.160 --> 09:30.330
With what? He touched your butt.

09:30.330 --> 09:33.070
Yeah, he touched it.

09:33.070 --> 09:34.700
You didn't like it, right?

09:34.700 --> 09:36.700
No, I didn't like it.

09:36.700 --> 09:41.710
If you don't like something,
you have to be tough and firm about it.

09:41.710 --> 09:43.040
Huh?

09:43.040 --> 09:46.010
Here, I'll show you how it's done.

09:46.010 --> 09:48.620
Hold on a second.

09:48.620 --> 09:53.050
Those guys are notorious thugs around here.

09:53.050 --> 09:55.720
If you make a mess of things, who knows
what they'll do to get back at you?

09:55.720 --> 09:58.790
- For all you know...
- There's nothing to worry about.

09:58.790 --> 10:01.280
Oh, w-wait!

10:03.130 --> 10:05.870
Refills?

10:05.870 --> 10:08.360
Yeah, please do.

10:14.010 --> 10:16.740
Wh-Why, you!

10:16.740 --> 10:18.950
Bitch!

10:18.950 --> 10:22.010
If you have any last words, say them now.

10:24.990 --> 10:27.650
So that's being tough and firm.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.320
I know!

10:44.370 --> 10:46.970
The owner sure comes up
with some crazy ideas.

10:46.970 --> 10:49.840
Asking us to work as guards, too.

10:49.840 --> 10:52.780
Well, thanks to that, we have
someplace to stay now, though,

10:52.780 --> 10:54.950
so that was a big help.

10:54.950 --> 10:57.350
A lot of things happened.

10:57.350 --> 10:59.220
Tired?

10:59.220 --> 11:00.920
Yes.

11:00.920 --> 11:03.920
Because there was a lot to remember.

11:03.920 --> 11:07.960
Like the names of the dishes and drinks.

11:07.960 --> 11:09.300
That's true.

11:09.300 --> 11:11.820
And also, being tough and firm.

11:13.130 --> 11:16.340
Being tough and firm when
there's something I don't like...

11:16.340 --> 11:18.860
You taught me that.

11:20.410 --> 11:22.240
Nadie?

12:02.950 --> 12:05.710
Welcome! Oh...

12:14.330 --> 12:17.500
Thank you for waiting.

12:17.500 --> 12:20.940
What are you doing here?

12:20.940 --> 12:23.870
That's my line.

12:23.870 --> 12:25.440
It's obvious, isn't it?

12:25.440 --> 12:29.340
- Working a part-time job.
- Same here, more or less.

12:29.340 --> 12:34.140
Come to think of it, you said you'd
lost your client, too, didn't you?

12:47.460 --> 12:49.100
That's right.

12:49.100 --> 12:52.000
Buy 3,000 shares of Albright.

12:52.000 --> 12:56.840
And to offset that, please sell
the shares of Pylon Corporation.

12:56.840 --> 12:58.770
Then I'll leave the rest to you.

13:01.210 --> 13:03.210
How about some lunch?

13:03.210 --> 13:05.380
They built a store nearby.

13:05.380 --> 13:07.480
It's supposed to be authentic tacos.

13:07.480 --> 13:10.120
Amigo Tacos...

13:10.120 --> 13:12.490
Could it be that you're not much of a fan?

13:12.490 --> 13:16.860
No, I love them.

13:16.860 --> 13:18.950
Be good and wait here.

13:25.870 --> 13:27.300
What's this?

13:27.300 --> 13:30.840
- You can sing our song, right?
- Yes...

13:30.840 --> 13:33.840
Go sing and distribute these.

13:33.840 --> 13:35.500
What?

13:39.910 --> 13:43.450
I'm going to drop by the bank,
so watch the place for me.

13:43.450 --> 13:45.150
Okay.

13:50.560 --> 13:52.860
You want to help me?

14:01.440 --> 14:03.460
You're very good at this.

14:07.580 --> 14:09.240
Welco...

14:19.320 --> 14:21.120
Go hide.

14:23.120 --> 14:28.400
♪ Taco, taco, tacos. Tasty tacos. ♪

14:28.400 --> 14:33.070
♪ The most awesome tacos are Amigo Tacos! ♪

14:33.070 --> 14:35.070
Teehee!

14:35.070 --> 14:37.240
Could I order here?

14:37.240 --> 14:39.070
Is our food ready yet?

14:39.070 --> 14:41.410
- Yes.
- Could I get a beer, too?

14:41.410 --> 14:43.070
Yes.

14:44.350 --> 14:46.610
I'd like a refill.

14:50.020 --> 14:52.320
Come on, you're taking too long.

14:52.320 --> 14:54.890
You're going to end up getting fired.

14:54.890 --> 14:56.880
Thank you for waiting.

14:59.430 --> 15:04.570
Humans are such selfish creatures, aren't they?

15:04.570 --> 15:08.970
They know you're the only one working in here,

15:08.970 --> 15:11.940
and yet, they keep making unreasonable demands.

15:11.940 --> 15:15.380
- Please enjoy.
- Wait.

15:15.380 --> 15:17.280
It's a tip.

15:23.020 --> 15:25.450
I've made up my mind, Ellis.

15:25.450 --> 15:30.120
I'll show you just how foolish human beings are.

15:30.120 --> 15:32.120
I don't need you to do that.

15:42.270 --> 15:45.540
Please don't shoot us!

15:45.540 --> 15:49.410
Let's have drinks in Hell, amigo.

15:57.990 --> 16:00.960
Service, please.

16:00.960 --> 16:03.460
What would you like to order?

16:03.460 --> 16:06.050
What I want to eat...

16:11.600 --> 16:13.590
...is you.

16:15.070 --> 16:17.170
What would you like to order?

16:17.170 --> 16:20.070
Let me think.

16:20.070 --> 16:24.110
What should I get?

16:24.110 --> 16:27.410
There are so many choices,
I can't make up my mind.

16:30.480 --> 16:34.050
Amigo Tacos. We have some specials going on.

16:34.050 --> 16:36.620
- Here you are.
- You...

16:36.620 --> 16:40.290
Huh?! I thought you were at the restaurant!

16:42.730 --> 16:45.100
You say that, but what about you?

16:48.100 --> 16:50.330
Thank you very much.

16:54.540 --> 16:57.480
We're alone now,

16:57.480 --> 16:59.280
Ellis.

17:00.450 --> 17:04.650
You look pretty nice in
that kind of outfit, too.

17:04.650 --> 17:08.560
Ah, it's great...

17:08.560 --> 17:10.490
It's great...

17:13.190 --> 17:16.220
I want to create a new world with you.

17:19.800 --> 17:23.500
A place where foolish beings
such as humans don't exist...

17:25.210 --> 17:27.640
A world that belongs to just the two of us.

17:36.150 --> 17:39.350
Humor me for just a little while.

17:39.350 --> 17:41.590
Just for a little while.

17:41.590 --> 17:44.250
Come on, Ellis...

17:55.840 --> 17:58.070
Ellis!

17:58.070 --> 17:59.730
You'll hit the cars.

18:03.680 --> 18:06.080
Give it back.

18:06.080 --> 18:08.150
Is it that precious to you?

18:08.150 --> 18:09.680
Give it back.

18:09.680 --> 18:13.420
Put an even lovelier
expression on your face for me.

18:13.420 --> 18:15.180
Take a look.

18:17.390 --> 18:20.430
Your treasure...

18:20.430 --> 18:22.260
Stop...

18:25.730 --> 18:31.570
If you don't like something,
you have to be tough and firm about it.

18:38.680 --> 18:40.510
She did it!

18:46.820 --> 18:48.550
Ellis?

18:55.600 --> 18:58.120
W-Wait...

18:59.470 --> 19:01.160
Uh-oh.

19:02.200 --> 19:04.740
That hurts...

19:04.740 --> 19:06.710
That hurts,

19:06.710 --> 19:08.400
Ellis.

19:15.280 --> 19:18.490
That's enough.

19:18.490 --> 19:20.250
Nadie...

19:21.620 --> 19:23.610
Leave the rest to me.

19:26.590 --> 19:28.430
Where's Lirio?

19:28.430 --> 19:30.200
Lirio's in the back.

19:30.200 --> 19:31.690
Got it.

19:33.900 --> 19:36.670
If you have any last words, say them now.

19:38.440 --> 19:41.340
You won't be able to kill me.

19:41.340 --> 19:42.810
Care to put it to the test?

19:42.810 --> 19:44.680
Ellis!

19:44.680 --> 19:48.820
You don't know where Wiñay Marka is.

19:48.820 --> 19:50.720
Isn't that right?

19:50.720 --> 19:57.790
You're just heading south,
driven by a vague urge.

19:57.790 --> 19:59.690
Am I wrong?

20:01.500 --> 20:07.770
But I know where Wiñay Marka is.

20:07.770 --> 20:11.570
If I were to die,

20:11.570 --> 20:15.240
you would never get there.

20:19.880 --> 20:21.780
Ellis...

20:25.290 --> 20:27.750
- No!
- Ellis...

20:27.750 --> 20:31.820
Thank you, Ellis. I love you!

20:36.300 --> 20:38.700
Follow me.

20:38.700 --> 20:41.670
I'll lead you to Wiñay Marka.

21:04.990 --> 21:09.860
To think Ellis would do such a thing to me...

21:16.970 --> 21:18.970
It's fine...

21:18.970 --> 21:22.010
This is just another part of who we are.

21:22.010 --> 21:23.880
Love is...

21:23.880 --> 21:26.680
...wonderful!

21:26.680 --> 21:28.580
Isn't it, though?

21:33.390 --> 21:36.290
This is in lieu of a parting gift.

21:40.390 --> 21:42.360
This is?

21:42.360 --> 21:44.920
The perfected sauce with honey in it.

21:47.470 --> 21:48.990
Thank you.

21:54.070 --> 21:59.910
Ellis, it's okay to get angry,
but pull your punches a little, okay?

21:59.910 --> 22:01.780
Angry?

22:03.380 --> 22:06.090
I see.

22:06.090 --> 22:08.920
So I got angry.

22:27.470 --> 22:29.410
On this day,

22:29.410 --> 22:33.810
for the first time, Ellis became
aware of the emotion called anger.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Owaranai natsu no you ni

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Chiranai hana no you ni

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Dakishimeta sono ude o

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Zutto hanasanaide ite yo

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Sugari-tsuite-mitemo

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
Mune wa mada chigau hakanasa de

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Toki no rizumu kazoeteru

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
Akai hoshi no yoru

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
Kiete-yuku nukumori

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
Tsunagi-tometai no yo

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
Hitomi tojita kimi o

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Akogare o kuri-kaeshi

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Doko e mo yukenaku-temo

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
Setsunasa no tachidomaru

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
Kono hito-toki ga futari no

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
Subete yo
